Third-party material

This product bundles third-party material under its own licenses, listed below. The per-file
list (author, source, license) is in assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Inter (assets/fonts/Inter-*.ttf) — SIL Open Font License 1.1. See assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt.
Showcase photographs by Ansel Adams, Dorothea Lange and NASA (docs/images/) — public domain. See assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

crates/raw/src/spectral_table.rs (lightcraft-raw) holds camera colour matrices derived from the
camera spectral sensitivities, training reflectances and model alias list of rawtoaces-data
(https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/rawtoaces-data, v1.1.0), an Academy Software
Foundation project licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and from the CIE 1931 colour-matching
functions it ships (CIE, CC-BY-4.0). The matrices were fitted by the LightCraft contributors
(2026) with tools/spectral_camera_table.py. See assets/ATTRIBUTION.md.

crates/inpaint (lightcraft-inpaint) ports the inpainting (PatchMatch completion) and Poisson membrane
fill code of PhotoCraft (https://github.com/storytold/photocraft, crates/algo/src/inpaint.rs and
poisson.rs), Copyright the PhotoCraft contributors, licensed under the MIT License or the Apache
License 2.0, at your option. The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026); each
ported file says so.

crates/segment (lightcraft-segment) ports the SAM 3 model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/sam3 and sam3_tracker),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and restructured; each ported file says so. Because of this, crates/segment is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE), not under the MIT option.

The SAM 3 weights are not part of Ember and are never distributed with it. A user downloads
the facebook/sam3 checkpoint only when they choose to (in the app, or by hand), under Meta's SAM
License (https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3/blob/main/LICENSE), a separate, non-OSI
licence. See docs/ai-masks.md.

crates/segment/src/dinov2.rs and dinov2_positions.rs adapt the DINOv2 ViT-S/14 architecture from
Meta's DINOv2 repository at commit 7764ea0f912e53c92e82eb78a2a1631e92725fc8, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2/blob/7764ea0f912e53c92e82eb78a2a1631e92725fc8/LICENSE).
Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
The files were modified by Ember contributors (2026): translated to Rust on Candle,
restricted to 224/518 inputs, with explicit validation & cached positional tables.
dinov2_input.rs independently implements bounded RGB8 preprocessing using the pinned
Meta evaluation transform as its policy reference. dinov2_inventory.rs records factual
tensor names, shapes & byte ranges from static checkpoint inspection; dinov2_artifact.rs
loads only exact size- and SHA-256-verified bytes. These additions are source-only,
with no production culling integration or qualified model accuracy.
DINOv2 weights are not distributed.

MediaPipe Face Landmarker v1 raw graph support is independently implemented in
crates/segment/src/mediapipe*.rs. Generated metadata records factual tensor names,
shapes, operators, options & byte ranges from the exact SHA-pinned task artifact;
no floating-point tensor values, model weights or training data are distributed.
The artifact's BlazeFace, FaceMesh-V2 & Blendshape model cards state Apache-2.0;
model-card URLs, artifact identity & qualification boundaries are retained in
docs/models/mediapipe-face-landmarker-v1-qualification.json.
The metadata inspector uses the public TensorFlow Lite schema at revision
e3388c0b93738d8d1a59211ffe2d0643da907291 (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/tensorflow/tflite-micro/blob/e3388c0b93738d8d1a59211ffe2d0643da907291/tensorflow/lite/schema/schema.fbs

MediaPipe image preprocessing, detector decoding, weighted NMS, face-crop projection,
landmark subset & blendshape labels in crates/segment/src/mediapipe_detector.rs,
mediapipe_input.rs, mediapipe_blendshapes.rs & mediapipe_photo.rs adapt Google MediaPipe
source at commit 458200ffced12a9db596ddf1cce3380ea05f71fb (Apache License 2.0):
https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe/tree/458200ffced12a9db596ddf1cce3380ea05f71fb
Copyright The MediaPipe Authors (2019–2025, as stated in source headers).
Modified by Ember contributors (2026): translated to bounded pure Rust/Candle,
restricted to still RGB8 images & exact v1 graph dimensions, with explicit validation,
stable score ties, floating-point bilinear sampling & read-only observation output.
Full license: docs/licenses/mediapipe-LICENSE.txt. Pinned source & artifact metadata:
docs/models/mediapipe-image-contract.md. No model weights or training data are distributed.

DINOv2 positional interpolation also follows PyTorch v2.4.0's native bicubic implementation
(https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.4.0/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/UpSample.cuh); its
BSD-style license notice is retained in docs/licenses/pytorch-bicubic-LICENSE.txt.

AI denoise weights are not part of Ember and are never distributed with it.
The default build offers user-supplied models only. The optional rawnind-model
feature offers a separately downloaded RawNIND UtNet2 Bayer checkpoint under
GPL-3.0 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html), after the user accepts its terms.
Commercial use is subject to those terms, including applicable source, licence and
notice obligations on redistribution. Enabling that offer in releases remains a
maintainer decision. The ONNX reader and CPU/GPU executor are our Rust implementation;
no darktable, RawSpeed, LibRaw or other GPL decoder/runtime code is included.

Builds made with craft-fonts (the optional CRAFT_FONTS_DIR build input; all official releases)
also embed the fonts listed in https://github.com/storytold/craft-fonts/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md
(the Japanese fonts BIZ UDPGothic, BIZ UDMincho and Shippori Mincho; the web build embeds only BIZ
UDPGothic Regular), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Release packages include each font's
licence as OFL-<family>.txt.

Place names for reverse geocoding (Photo > Fill Location from GPS) are not part of LightCraft and
are never distributed with it. On the user's request (Photo > Download Place Names) the app
downloads cities15000.zip, admin1CodesASCII.txt and countryInfo.txt from GeoNames
(https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/) into the settings folder. GeoNames data is licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/);
attribution: "GeoNames, geonames.org". The lookup code (crates/geocode) is our own.

FFmpeg (LGPL sidecar, video)

Ember reads video (probe and poster frames) by running the FFmpeg and FFprobe command-line programs as separate child processes
(crates/video, through rightkit-ffmpeg). FFmpeg is Copyright (c) the FFmpeg developers and is licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later (https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html). The programs are not part of this repository and are not
linked into Ember. Release bundles ship only builds that the rightkit-ffmpeg approved catalog lists: configured with
--disable-gpl --disable-nonfree --disable-autodetect (no GPL and no non-free code), identified by content SHA-256 and checked
before they run. Ember has no video support where they are not bundled (Linux ships without video for now); see docs/video.md.

Source offer: for every release bundle that includes these programs, Orthic Labs offers the corresponding FFmpeg source code, the
build recipe, and the licence texts of the components statically linked into the shipped build (all recorded in the
rightkit-ffmpeg catalog entry for that build), on request, for at least three years after the release, at no more than the cost of
distribution. Request them by opening an issue at https://github.com/Orthic-Labs/ember. The release bundle carries the FFmpeg
licence notice beside the programs. Nothing in Ember's own MIT or Apache-2.0 licence changes the terms of the LGPL for FFmpeg.
